{title: Lo! He Comes with Clouds Descending}
{artist: Charles Wesley}
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 84}

Verse 1
[G]Lo! he comes with [C]clouds de[G]scending, [Em]once for [C]favored [D]sinners [G]slain;
thousand thousand [C]saints at[G]tending [Em]swell the [C]triumph [D]of his [G]train:
alle[C]luia! alle[G]luia! [D]God appears on [G]earth to reign.

Verse 2
[G]Ev'ry eye shall now behold [C]Him Robed in [Em]dreadful majesty; [C]Those [D]who set [G]at
naught and [C]sold Him, Pierced [Em]and nailed [C]Him [D]to the tree, [G]Deeply
wailing, deeply [D]wailing, deeply wailing, Shall [G]the true Messiah see.

Verse 3
[G]Ev'ry island, sea, and mountain, [C]Heav'n and earth, [Em]shall flee [C]away; [D]All who [G]hate
Him must, confounded, [C]Hear the [Em]trump proclaim the [C]day: [D]Come to judgment! [G]Come
to judgment! [D]Come to judgment! Come [G]to judgment! Come away!

Verse 4
[G]Now redemption, long expected, [C]See in [Em]solemn pomp [C]appear; [D]All [G]His
saints, by [C]man rejected, [Em]Now shall meet [C]Him [D]in the [G]air:
Hallelujah! Hallelujah! [D]Hallelujah! See the day [G]of God appear!

Verse 5
[G]Answer Thine own bride and [C]Spirit, Hasten, [Em]Lord, the [C]gen'ral doom! [D]The [G]new
Heav'n and [C]earth inherit, Take [Em]Thy pining [C]exiles [D]home: All creation, [G]all
creation, all [D]creation, Travails! groans! and [G]bids Thee come!
